4.Modify your decision table from Task 1 to include an additional rule: the coupon cannot be used more than twice by the same user. Update the table and explain how this new rule changes the possible outcomes.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Add a column for 'Coupon Usage Count' and adjust the actions accordingly.</em>
Answer :

The coupon will be accepted only if all four conditions are satisfied:
User is logged in.
a)Cart value is above ₹500.
b)Coupon is not expired.
c)Coupon usage count is less than 2.

Possible Outcomes
>Logged in + Cart > ₹500 + Coupon valid + Usage count 0 → Accept
>Logged in + Cart > ₹500 + Coupon valid + Usage count 1 → Accept
>Logged in + Cart > ₹500 + Coupon valid + Usage count 2 or more → Reject
>If the user is not logged in → Reject
>If cart value is ₹500 or less → Reject
>If the coupon is expired → Reject

Effect of the new rule: The coupon can now be used maximum twice by the same user. After the second use, further attempts are rejected.
